SUMMARY:Planting Bulbs in the Fall for Spring Glory
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging demo on all things bulbs!\nPlanting bulbs in the fall will bring glorious rewards in your spring garden. Learn what to plant from tulips to garlic\, how to plant them and yes\, even a few pointers on squirrels!\n \nWednesday\, September 23\, 6:30 to 8 p.m.\nPublic $20\, TBG Members $15 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Joanna Blanchard\nJoanna Blanchard has been a member of the Toronto Master Gardeners for just over 15 years. She was introduced to horticulture and gardening almost from birth\, since her father was a botany professor and her mother a plant pathologist! Throughout her childhood the talk at the dinner table was often about plants\, and visiting gardens and garden centres were part of daily life. Despite her best teenaged efforts to repel the gardening bug she was unsuccessful! \n \nAs soon as Joanna came to Canada from the UK\, she got going with houseplants\, flower boxes and books about plants. Moving into a house with a garden expanded the possibilities\, and her gardening efforts have progressed from there. \n \nAfter several decades of gardening successes and many failures\, she loves to share her passion for all things horticultural. \n \nJoanna is a past coordinator of the Toronto Master Gardeners and past president of the Leaside Garden Society. She is a member of the Greater Toronto Bulb Society\, and has a particular love for the early-spring bulbs that brighten our lives after a long\, cold winter.\n \nAbout Toronto Master Gardeners\nToronto Master Gardeners (TMG) is a volunteer not-for-profit organization that shares current\, science-based horticultural information with the gardening public through various channels\, including in person\, in print\, through the media\, and online. Committed volunteers support and inspire the community\, and continually update the sound knowledge required to help them. Learn more and ask your questions Toronto Master Gardeners – Helping Gardeners.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/planting-bulbs-in-the-fall-for-spring-glory/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
