SUMMARY:En Plein Air Connections: Botanical Watercolour in Bloom
DESCRIPTION:Experience the Toronto Botanical Garden through the art of watercolour in this guided outdoor workshop!\nUsing freshly gathered blooms and botanical patterns as inspiration\, you’ll explore approachable painting techniques while incorporating moments of mindfulness that encourage a deeper connection with the natural world. Suitable for all experience levels\, this relaxed workshop offers personalized instruction in a welcoming and supportive environment.\n \nAll materials are provided.\n \nPlease note: This is an outdoor class that requries about a 10-minute walk with some steep slopes to get to the location. In the case of poor weather\, the class will be moved indoors. Please arrive promptly for 1 p.m. We will gather in the Lobby before heading to the outdoor workshop spot.\n \nThursday\, October 15\, 1 to 3:30 p.m.\nPublic $80\, TBG Members $75 (plus applicable taxes and fees).\n \nAbout Aggie Armstrong\nAggie Armstrong is a Filipino-Canadian artist living and working in Ontario. Working primarily in painting while incorporating hand embroidery and textile elements\, she creates layered work inspired by everyday experiences\, personal history\, and the ways we make sense of the world around us.\n \nHer work has been exhibited across Canada\, the United States\, and France\, and she has exhibited at The Artist Project in Toronto since 2022. In 2023\, she was commissioned to create the official poster for the Royal Agricultural Winter Fair\, and in 2022 she was an artist-in-residence at Château Orquevaux in France. Her work has also been featured in British Vogue\, Art Seen Magazine\, CTV News\, CP24 Breakfast\, the Create!\, and Colour Me Happy podcasts.\n \nAlongside her studio practice\, Aggie teaches watercolour workshops throughout the GTA and Southwestern Ontario\, creating welcoming\, approachable experiences that help people build confidence and discover the joy of painting and creativity.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\n \nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/en-plein-air-connections-botanical-watercolour-in-bloom/
