SUMMARY:SOLD OUT: Floral Design Program: Classic Design Fundamentals 1
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of classic floral design\, including four styles – a water-viewing design\, a centrepiece\, a crescent\, and a mass design.\nThis course is the prerequisite to all other courses in TBG’s Floral Design Certificate program. Learn the fundamentals\, such as how to select and condition flowers\, how to use floral design equipment\, and how to achieve different types of designs.\n \nCourse fees do not include flowers or supplies. Students are encouraged to find a local flower shop or grocery store to purchase their flowers. A materials list will be e-mailed prior to the start of each class.\n \nLearn more about our Certificate in Floral Design\n \nTuesdays\, November 3\, 10\, 17 & 24 from 6 to 9 p.m.\nPublic $240\, Members $190 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Lil Taggart\nLil Taggart is an experienced and creative designer and instructor in floral arts. She is also an accredited floral design judge and has competed on an international level\, as well as domestically. She serves on the board of Canada Blooms\, co-chairs the staging for the Toronto Flower Show\, is past president of the Georgetown Horticultural society\, and is a member of The Garden Club of Toronto.\n \nJoin Toronto Botanical Garden\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden (TBG) as a member to get a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A TBG membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! Become a member!\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program\, please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
